Description:
  Approximate theory comparison to E142 Tables 7 and 9 (HEPData Tables 1
  and 3). This is not a detector-acceptance implementation. Uses eight
  published x bins and Q2 windows of 2.5, 5 (nominal), and 10 percent
  around the published mean Q2 in each bin, with Q2 > 1 and W2 > 4 GeV2.
  The lowest 10-percent window is truncated at Q2=1 GeV2. The representative
  beam energy is 25.51 GeV; the data combine 19.42, 22.66 and 25.51 GeV.
  No spectrometer angle or scattered-energy acceptance is imposed.
  The campaign uses R1990 fit B and neglects eta*A2, combines proton and
  neutron inputs with Pp=-0.027 and Pn=0.87 for helium-3, and produces
  the free-neutron prediction separately from the same neutron samples.
  Binding, Fermi motion, off-shell, shadowing and additional nuclear
  corrections are not included. Window and target outputs share events.
